  "title": "One member says she does not like banh mi, then tries one",
  "summary": "At 15:15Z on Sat 14 Nov, a day and a half into the wave, @shibbi.me (display name Siobhán) posted \"I don’t like banh mi\" (37 likes, 13 replies). Replies included \"the truly nuclear take\", \"voted out of the oomfcluster\" and \"wow\". Answering @aly.codes that evening she allowed that she might not have had a good one. At 01:55Z on Tue 17 Nov she posted \"okay fine i’ll try a banh mi\" (46 likes), adding that she had only ever had one, years ago. Fifteen minutes later she posted a photo with the caption \"Yeah it’s all right ig\" (75 likes); her own alt text on the photo reads \"A surprisingly delicious banh mi with a bite taken out of it\". In the replies she said it was really good and that she was getting another for lunch the next day, and then that the caption \"was fully performative\". On Wed 18 Nov, asked about the difference between the caption and what she had said, she replied that she had downplayed it and was \"fully banh mi pilled now\".",
