  "sensitive": "No post on this card carries a flag from the tool. Where the banh mi wave came from is not for the show. Other posts in the window by some of the same accounts frame it around trans women, and a thread about it turns to hormone medication and nudes (R10: gender identity, health, sexuality). The digest flags several of those posts one by one, and flags the whole thread \"why is everyone banh mi posting?\" (story 12, which also holds the \"banhmi-contagion\" graph the build bot made): nothing from that thread is on this card and the check refuses it. None of this should be used as explanation or background; the show cannot say why the wave started beyond what the posts listed here say. On this card specifically: (1) \"it changed my neural chemistry\" reads as a figure of speech about a sandwich and not as a statement about health; left for the reviewer to judge. (2) Left out of these threads: a reply asking whether she has a genetic taste trait, a reply and answer that name where she lives and the shop, and a reply from an account that spoke in the previous episode. (3) @aly.codes: see the note on the card talk-banh-mi-how-it-spread. (4) @emilia.bsky.social is outside the cluster's membership. (5) @huwupy.kawaii.social has 7,191 followers. (6) The same thread contains a separate exchange about where the best one is sold: card talk-banh-mi-ideal-shop."
